The error message you are encountering, "The method listener(Object) is ambiguous for the type SimpleStepBuilder<UserInfo, UserInfo>", suggests that there is a type conflict when adding your custom listener `StopListener` to the step. This often occurs when the framework cannot determine the correct overload of the listener method to use due to ambiguous types.

To resolve this, you can explicitly specify the type of the listener you are adding. Since `StopListener` extends `StepListenerSupport`, you should utilize the appropriate method that takes a `StepListener` as a parameter. Here is how you can modify your code:

```java
@Bean
public Step dataFilterStep() {
    return stepBuilderFactory.get("dataFilterStep")
            .<UserInfo, UserInfo>chunk(10)
            .reader(dataFilterItemReader())
            .processor(dataFilterItemProcessor())
            .writer(dataFilterWriter())
            .listener((StepExecutionListener) new StopListener())  // Explicitly cast to StepExecutionListener
            .build();
}
```

By explicitly casting `StopListener` to `StepExecutionListener`, you clarify to the compiler which method overload you intend to use, thereby eliminating the ambiguity.

