[SO-22262803] Q: jquery giving TypeError getting elements from wrapped set
A: <p><code>addClass</code> is a jQuery method. It can only be called on jQuery objects. When you call <code>[0]</code> or <code>.get(0)</code> on your jQuery object, you are fetching the underlying DOM element. That object doesn't support the jQuery methods.</p>

<p>You should call <code>addClass</code> on the jQuery object itself:</p>

<p><code>img[alt].addClass('my-new-class');</code>.</p>

<p>If you only want to add a class to the first image with an <code>alt</code> attribute, you could change the jQuery selector to <code>$('img[alt]:first')</code>.</p>


